/-!
# Arithmetic of Square-Root Precision

Umbrella for the arithmetic of precision: precision classes of statements about weights and the
count; the count for `Λ` in each half and its exponent; the battery as a classification; the
deciding-input theorem and the precision-blindness of producers; the integrality lattice of the
horizon and the integrality exponent; integer Dirichlet polynomials at arithmetic points; the
Liouville twin as a ratio of horizon torsions; the Chebyshev ledger of where precision is lost;
calibration of precision exponents on curve data; the gauge stabilizer of the count; the precision
ledger; the vanishing forced by sup-norm ceilings; majorants, minorants and abscissas of one-signed
perturbations; the separation of prime logarithms and the two-prime non-aliasing law; inversion of monotone errors
at Mertens precision, the split of the Stirling error and the arithmetic Chebyshev ledger; the precision-exactness of tower
positivity and the window law of finite-aperture positivity; the successor modulo the square-root
class. See `ArithmeticOfSquareRootPrecision/README.md`.
-/
